# VENTION-SDLC-MANAGED:BEGIN
#
# Everything between BEGIN / END is framework-managed and rewritten on every
# `vsdlc install`. Add your team's rules OUTSIDE these markers — they will be
# preserved byte-for-byte across upgrades.
#
# Claude Code copies matching paths into each new worktree. Only
# gitignored/untracked paths are candidates; tracked files arrive with the
# checkout.
#
# This block covers only what vsdlc itself writes, for the tools it supports
# (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, VS Code Copilot). Config for anything else —
# another assistant, your editor, personal tooling — belongs OUTSIDE the
# markers, where it is preserved.
#
# --- MCP servers + local tooling config ---------------------------------
/.mcp.json
/.mise.toml
/.vsdlc/workspace.local.toml
/.vsdlc/custom/*.user.toml
/.vsdlc/scripts/
# --- per-tool config vsdlc writes (metrics hooks, skills) ---------------
# `.claude/` is path-precise, NOT wholesale: a `/.claude/` pattern would also
# match `settings.local.json` — user-owned, and Claude Code copies it itself
# behind a guard against resurrecting revoked permissions — plus
# `scheduled_tasks.lock`, which is runtime state. The other tool directories
# hold only framework-written files, so a directory pattern is safe there.
/.claude/settings.json
/.claude/skills/
/.claude/commands/opsx/
/.agents/
/.cursor/
/.codex/
/.github/
# --- BMAD module workspace ----------------------------------------------
/_bmad/*
# VENTION-SDLC-MANAGED:END
